  "title": "Chulalongkorn (Rama V)",
  "summary": "Chulalongkorn (Rama V) became king of Siam in 1868 at age 15, after the death of his father Mongkut, and reigned until 1910. His reign brought centralised, modernising reforms. One of his major achievements was ending slavery step by step, from a decree of 1874 to the Slave Abolition Act of 1905.",
